Rather than relying on central authorities or external consensus layers, CVP records demonstrate priority and authenticity through direct mathematical proof. A CVP record combines payload content, spatial placement, governance dictionaries, and object linkages into a deterministic composite key. Signed cryptographically and linked sequentially to its immediate predecessor (prev: "GENESIS" through seq N), a CVP record cannot be backdated, reordered, or forged.

This architectural foundation underpins the multi-layer ingestion engine that automates data capture from physical environments directly into IPFS storage.

2. Autonomous Ingestion Architecture: "Det Levende Arkivet"

System Operational Context

To transition IPFS from a manual file-upload destination into a real-time, autonomous record-keeping infrastructure, the Commons Vector Protocol integrates "Det Levende Arkivet" (The Living Archive). Manual file uploads introduce operational friction, human delay, and recording bias. Det Levende Arkivet operates as an automated multi-layer pipeline that captures physical real-world inputs, normalizes them using artificial intelligence, structures them against standardized trust dictionaries, and pins them cryptographically to the IPFS network.

