The CVP Insertion Protocol

A core feature of CVP is the Insertion Protocol, which allows complex documents to reference external instruments without duplicating raw payload data. Because referenced .car records are content-addressed and immutable, referencing an instrument by its composite key incorporates its verifiable state into the host document.

1. Inline Text Reference Syntax

In unstructured text or markdown documents, instruments are referenced using canonical short codes or URI formats:

* Standard Inline: [See Instrument #003 — Fingerprint — composite key: a4f9c2e8d1b7...]
* Abbreviated Inline: [Inst. #003 — Fingerprint — a4f9c2e8]
* Canonical URI Syntax: car://003-fingerprint, car://003-fingerprint@commons-vector-v1, or car://a4f9c2e8d1b7...

2. Structured JSON Insertion Syntax

Within JSON documents, insertions are declared using standardized reference objects inside an insertions array, complete with optional metadata fields:

{
 "insertions": [
 {
 "car": "003",
 "label": "Fingerprint",
 "composite": "a4f9c2e8d1b72e3a1f8c9b0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f6a8c0d2e4f",
 "cid": "bafkreibiometricfingerprintcidexample",
