CVP does not assert false claims of overriding state, court, or statutory jurisdiction. Cryptographic priority proves content immutability, signature authenticity, and timestamped prior art; it does not replace statutory land registries, confer legal immunity, or enforce external legal mandates. CVP serves as an immutable, tamper-evident record of claims and prior art that external legal and judicial systems can evaluate as unalterable factual evidence.

