text{seq } N-1). * event: An upper-case event type string (e.g., MASTER_TRUST_INDEX_V2_PUBLISHED). * timestamp: An ISO 8601 formatted timestamp string. The chain originates at sequence zero (seq: 0), where the genesis record assigns its previous link to the canonical string prev: "GENESIS". Because each sequence's composite key incorporates its vector definitions and signature envelope, altering any historical record invalidates every subsequent link in the provenance chain. +----------------------------+ +----------------------------+ | Sequence 001 (Genesis) | | Sequence 002 | | CID: bafy...5zbfe | | CID: bafy...gxviq | | Spatial: ...:witness:1 | | Spatial: ...:witness:2 | | Rule: witness:true | | Rule: witness:true | | Composite: 0x1A2B... | | Composite: 0x3C4D... | | Prev: "GENESIS" |<------+ Prev: "0x1A2B..." | +----------------------------+ +----------------------------+ ^ | +-------------+--------------+ | Sequence 003 | | CID: bafy...xjm2y | | Spatial: ...:biometric | | Rule: biometric:true | | Composite: 0x5E6F... | | Prev: "0x3C4D..." | +----------------------------+ The next section demonstrates how this vector framework is instantiated within native .car file structures and verified using open-source tools. 4. Native .car Format, Insertion Protocol & Verification Engine Strategic Value of the .car Architecture The Commons Vector Protocol adopts .car (Content Addressable Archive / Record) as its native file format, metadata schema, and namespace structure. Rather than relying on chain-specific naming services (such as .eth or .sol), CVP uses .car as a portable, chain-agnostic container standard. A .car or .car.json object is fully self-describing. It encapsulates raw content references, vector placement, dictionary links, composite cryptographic keys, Ed25519 signatures, and sequence links within a single portable payload that can be stored on IPFS, transmitted via email, archived offline, or embedded inside other records. JSON Record Schema Template The 